note('After pass 19, derived additional weight-only evidence. Exact Gaussian SwiGLU Hessian / gain-matching solves were mostly orthogonal to known useful directions, so not a reliable correction prior. Functional writer covariances weighting Δdown and Δo by non-white base-input moments confirmed the coherent mid-layer subspace. The gated lift of Δup through the base down writer is a partially independent view of those same modes. Corroboration from late tied-embedding readouts was positive but diffuse; analytically averaging query variance gave near-identical attention-tilt drift. A new more selective sign signal is the first-order attention writer change -ΔO repeat(V diag(RMSNorm) c) for a medical-question versus ordinary-question embedding contrast c. It points partly along the existing successful vector, with similar signs across symptom/medication cue sets and damped linear transports. This is a weight contraction, not a token forward pass.')